---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/*
 * Sections are defined once and rendered twice — as the contents list and as
 * the body — so the two cannot drift apart as clauses are added.
 *
 * "Last updated" is a constant. It was previously new Date(), which meant the
 * date advanced on every deploy: a legal document appearing to have been
 * reviewed when nothing had been read.
 *
 * TO BE FILLED IN BEFORE THIS IS RELIED ON:
 *   - the CAC registration number.
 *   - a registered office address.
 *
 * The contracting entity is AZAP Operations Limited, confirmed by the founders
 * on 2026-09-09. The footer previously said "AZAP Technologies Inc.", which was
 * never the registered company and carried a US suffix.
 *
 * Not drafted by a lawyer. LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md carries legal review as an open
 * P0 alongside NDPC registration and a named DPO.
 */

const LAST_UPDATED = '9 September 2026';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'about',
    title: 'Who we are and what these terms cover',
    body: [
      'AZAP is a service operated by <strong class="text-ink">AZAP Operations Limited</strong>, a company registered in Nigeria. We introduce people who need work doing in their homes or premises to independent tradespeople and household professionals, and coordinate that work by telephone.',
      'These terms apply when you book through this website, when you speak to us on the telephone about a booking, and when you use this website generally. By making a booking you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not book.',
      'We have written these terms in plain language. Where something is a limitation rather than a promise, we have said so directly instead of burying it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'definitions',
    title: 'Definitions',
    body: [
      '<strong class="text-ink">"AZAP", "we", "us", "our"</strong> means AZAP Operations Limited, the company that operates the AZAP service.',
      '<strong class="text-ink">"You"</strong> means the person making a booking or using this website.',
      '<strong class="text-ink">"Pro"</strong> means an independent tradesperson or household professional we introduce to you. Pros are not employees, agents or partners of AZAP.',
      '<strong class="text-ink">"Job"</strong> means the work you and a pro agree they will carry out.',
      '<strong class="text-ink">"Booking"</strong> means a request you submit asking us to find you a pro.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'eligibility',
    title: 'Who can use AZAP',
    body: [
      'You must be at least 18 years old and legally able to enter into a contract. If you are booking on behalf of a company, a landlord, an estate or another person, you confirm you are authorised to do so and to give us access details for the property.',
      'You must be the occupier or owner of the property, or have the occupier or owner\'s permission for the work to be carried out.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'what-we-do',
    title: 'What AZAP does, and what it does not do',
    body: [
      '<strong class="text-ink">We do:</strong> take your booking, telephone you to confirm the details, find a pro we have checked who is willing and available to take the job, tell you who is coming, and telephone you afterwards to confirm the work was carried out. We keep a record of all of it.',
      '<strong class="text-ink">We do not:</strong> carry out any work ourselves; employ, supervise, direct or manage the pros; set, negotiate or control the price of any job; supply tools, parts or materials; take payment for any job; hold money on your behalf; or guarantee the quality, timeliness or outcome of any work.',
      'Pros decide for themselves whether to accept a job we offer them, how to carry it out, and what to charge. That independence is deliberate and it is central to how this service works.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'where',
    title: 'Where we operate',
    body: [
      'We currently serve Enugu, Nigeria, and we open one area at a time. If your address falls outside the area we cover, we will tell you on the confirmation call rather than send someone who cannot reasonably reach you.',
      'We may change the areas we serve at any time.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'booking',
    title: 'How a booking works',
    body: [
      'You submit a booking telling us what you need, where, and roughly when. Submitting a booking costs you nothing and does not commit you to anything.',
      'A booking is a request, not a confirmed appointment. Nothing is confirmed until we have spoken to you by telephone and told you that a pro is coming. We may be unable to find a pro for a particular job, time or location, and if so we will tell you.',
      'We may decline or cancel a booking at our discretion, including where we cannot verify the details, where the address is outside our service area, where we have no suitable pro available, or where we believe the request is not genuine.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'contract',
    title: 'Who your contract is with',
    body: [
      '<strong class="text-ink">Your contract for the work itself is with the pro, not with AZAP.</strong> When you agree a price and a scope of work with a pro, that agreement is between the two of you.',
      'These terms govern your use of AZAP\'s introduction and coordination service. They do not govern the work, and AZAP is not a party to the agreement you make with your pro.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'vetting',
    title: 'What we check about pros, and what we do not',
    body: [
      'Before a pro can take work through AZAP we verify four things: their National Identity Number and identity document, a bank account held in their own name, a named guarantor we can contact, and a photograph. We meet pros in person before adding them.',
